⍝ ZZ66_Regression.tc
⍝ ══════════════════

⍝@ test3.

      ⍝ bug-apl@gnu.org, Bugs9 (Blake McBride): regression coverage for the
      ⍝ critical/high severity findings below. See SVN log for details.

      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      ⍝ #1: Archive.cc next_ravel_Value() vs next_ravel_Pointer() -- )SAVE/
      ⍝ )LOAD used to silently collapse every nesting depth >=3 down to 2.
      X←⊂⊂1 2
      Y←⊂1 2
      Z←⊂⊂⊂1 2
      ≡X
3
      ≡Y
2
      ≡Z
4
      )SAVE /tmp/ZZ66_save_test
20⁰-⁰-⁰  ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰) 
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS
      )LOAD /tmp/ZZ66_save_test
SAVED 20⁰-⁰-⁰ ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰)
      ≡X
3
      ≡Y
2
      ≡Z
4

      ⍝ #2: A⍸B integer overflow -> heap overflow, SIGSEGV. Must now be a
      ⍝ clean WS FULL instead of writing past the (wrongly-sized) result.
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ characters beyond ⎕AV are a GNU APL extension; ⍤ ⍣ ⍸ ≢ are not in IBM APL2
      ⍸ 4 ⍴ 4611686018427387904
WS FULL
      ⍸4⍴4611686018427387904
      ^

      ⍝ #3: 1 ⎕TF inverse rank/shape parsing had no overflow bound --
      ⍝ a claimed rank/shape item could wrap and silently misparse.
      1 ⎕TF 'CX 65536 a'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      1 ⎕TF 'CX 65536 a'
      ^ ^
      )SIC

      ⍝ #4: CDR CHAR8 decode sign-extended bytes 128-255.
      ⎕UCS 12 ⎕CR 11 ⎕CR 'AéB'
65 233 66

      ⍝ #5: CDR nested CHAR32 scalar read big-endian, written little-endian.
      ⎕UCS ⊃12 ⎕CR 11 ⎕CR ((⎕UCS 300) 1)
300 

      ⍝ #6: 1 ⎕TF of an empty numeric array emitted a record its own
      ⍝ inverse rejected (missing the shape/data separator).
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      A←⍳0
      T←1 ⎕TF 'A'
      ⎕EX 'A'
1
      1 ⎕TF T
A
      ⍴A
0

      ⍝ #7 / #11: empty value built by a loop that never runs kept the
      ⍝ default numeric prototype instead of the intended one.
      B←''
      T←1 ⎕TF 'B'
      ⎕EX 'B'
1
      1 ⎕TF T
B
      B≡''
1
      (⎕JSON '""')≡''
1

      ⍝ #8: 2 ⎕TF of an empty char array dropped both shape and enclosure;
      ⍝ separately, a length-1 nested vector lost one enclosure level
      ⍝ (relied on strand notation to re-create it, which needs >=2 items).
      C←2 0⍴'a'
      2 ⎕TF 'C'
C←2 0⍴' '
      NN←,⊂⊂''
      ≡NN
3
      T←2 ⎕TF 'NN'
      ⎕EX 'NN'
1
      ⍎T
      ≡NN
3

      ⍝ #9: A⍒B (collating grade down) broke ties in descending index
      ⍝ order instead of ascending.
      N←4 1⍴'abab'
      'ab'⍒N
2 4 1 3

      ⍝ #10: empty JSON object serialised to '}' -- invalid JSON, and its
      ⍝ own output no longer parsed.
      2 ⎕JSON ⎕JSON '{}'
{}

      )ERASE X Y Z A B C N NN T
      )DROP /tmp/ZZ66_save_test
³

      ]NEXTFILE
